    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2023-june/q4",
      "question": "<p><strong>In this question you must show all stages of your working.</strong></p><p><strong>Solutions relying entirely on calculator technology are not acceptable.</strong></p><p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\\in\\mathbb R\"></span></p><p>Given that</p><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f&#x27;(x)=2x+\\frac{1}{2}\\cos x\"></span></li><li>the curve has a stationary point with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> coordinate <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span></li><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> is small</li></ul><ol class=\"parts\"><li>use the small angle approximation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\cos x\"></span> to estimate the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> to 3 decimal places. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>The point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P(0,3)\"></span> lies on <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span></p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>Find the equation of the tangent to the curve at <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"P\"></span>, giving your answer in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=mx+c\"></span>, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"m\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"c\"></span> are constants to be found. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
