    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2023-june/q5",
      "question": "<p>A continuous curve has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\"></span>.</p><p>The table shows corresponding values of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span> for this curve, where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are constants.</p><table class=\"practice-table\"><tr><td><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span></td><td>3</td><td>3.2</td><td>3.4</td><td>3.6</td><td>3.8</td><td>4</td></tr><tr><td><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span></td><td><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span></td><td>16.8</td><td><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span></td><td>20.2</td><td>18.7</td><td>13.5</td></tr></table><p>The trapezium rule is used, with all the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span> values in the table, to find an approximate area under the curve between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=3\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=4\"></span></p><p>Given that this area is 17.59</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a+2b=51\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>Given also that the sum of all the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span> values in the table is 97.2</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li>find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
