    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2023-june/q8",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:140mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-2023-june/q08-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 1. Plan view of a stage, not accurately drawn: front of stage at the top, back of stage at the bottom. Straight line AOG of length 15 m along the back; triangles ABO and GFO on either side; sector OCDEO of a circle centre O with angle COE 2.3 rad and arc CDE 27.6 m; dashed lines OC and OE.\"></figure><p>Figure 1 shows the plan view of a stage.</p><p>The plan view shows two congruent triangles <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABO\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"GFO\"></span> joined to a sector <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"OCDEO\"></span> of a circle, centre <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"O\"></span>, where</p><ul><li>angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"COE\"></span> = 2.3 radians</li><li>arc length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"CDE\"></span> = <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"27.6\\,\\mathrm m\"></span></li><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AOG\"></span> is a straight line of length <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"15\\,\\mathrm m\"></span></li></ul><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"OC=12\\,\\mathrm m\"></span>. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>Show that the size of angle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"AOB\"></span> is 0.421 radians correct to 3 decimal places. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>Given that the total length of the front of the stage, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"BCDEF\"></span>, is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"35\\,\\mathrm m\"></span>,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>find the total area of the stage, giving your answer to the nearest square metre. <span class=\"marks\">(6)</span></li></ol>",
