      "question": "<p>The first three terms of a geometric sequence are</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3k+4\\qquad12-3k\\qquad k+16\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> is a constant.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span> satisfies the equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"3k^2-62k+40=0\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>Given that the sequence converges,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"2\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>, giving a reason for your answer,</li><li>find the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"S_\\infty\"></span></li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li></ol>",
