    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2023-june/q11",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:100mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-2023-june/q11-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 2. Graph of log10 V against t: a straight line with negative gradient passing through (0, 3) and (10, 2.79).\"></figure><p>The value, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span> pounds, of a mobile phone, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> months after it was bought, is modelled by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"V=ab^t\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are constants.</p><p>Figure 2 shows the linear relationship between <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\log_{10}V\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span>.</p><p>The line passes through the points (0, 3) and (10, 2.79) as shown.</p><p>Using these points,</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>find the initial value of the phone, <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li><li>find a complete equation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"V\"></span> in terms of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span>, giving the exact value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and giving the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> to 3 significant figures. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>Exactly 2 years after it was bought, the value of the phone was £320</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>Use this information to evaluate the reliability of the model. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
