      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2023-june/q12",
      "question": "<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"y=\\sin x\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> is measured in radians.</p><p>Use differentiation from first principles to show that</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\frac{\\mathrm dy}{\\mathrm dx}=\\cos x\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>You may</p><ul><li>use without proof the formula for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\sin(A\\pm B)\"></span></li><li>assume that as <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"h\\to0\"></span>, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{\\sin h}{h}\\to1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\dfrac{\\cos h-1}{h}\\to0\"></span></li></ul><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
