    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2023-june/q13",
      "question": "<p>On a roller coaster ride, passengers travel in carriages around a track.</p><p>On the ride, carriages complete multiple circuits of the track such that</p><ul><li>the maximum vertical height of a carriage above the ground is <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"60\\,\\mathrm m\"></span></li><li>a carriage starts a circuit at a vertical height of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"2\\,\\mathrm m\"></span> above the ground</li><li>the ground is horizontal</li></ul><p>The vertical height, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"H\\,\\mathrm m\"></span>, of a carriage above the ground, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> seconds after the carriage starts the first circuit, is modelled by the equation</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"H=a-b(t-20)^2\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"a\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"b\"></span> are positive constants.</p><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Find a complete equation for the model. <span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li><li>Use the model to determine the height of the carriage above the ground when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t=40\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol><p>In an alternative model, the vertical height, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"H\\,\\mathrm m\"></span>, of a carriage above the ground, <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"t\"></span> seconds after the carriage starts the first circuit, is given by</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"H=29\\cos(9t+\\alpha)^\\circ+\\beta\\qquad0\\leqslant\\alpha&lt;360^\\circ\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\beta\"></span> are constants.</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>Find a complete equation for the alternative model. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>Given that the carriage moves continuously for 2 minutes,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li>give a reason why the alternative model would be more appropriate. <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
        "<figure class=\"exam-solution-source\" style=\"margin:2mm 0\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-2023-june/q13-ms-p28-1.svg\" alt=\"Official mark scheme for original question 13; source page 28, segment 1 of 2. Includes the original working, marks, alternative methods and examiner guidance in source order.\" style=\"display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-width:100%\"></figure>",
