    {
      "id": "exam/edexcel-9ma0-01-2023-june/q15",
      "question": "<p>A curve has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\mathrm f(x)\"></span>, where</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f(x)=\\frac{7x\\mathrm e^x}{\\sqrt{\\mathrm e^{3x}-2}}\\qquad x&gt;\\ln\\sqrt[3]{2}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><ol class=\"parts\"><li>Show that<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"\\mathrm f&#x27;(x)=\\frac{7\\mathrm e^x\\left(\\mathrm e^{3x}(2-x)+Ax+B\\right)}{2\\left(\\mathrm e^{3x}-2\\right)^{\\frac{3}{2}}}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B\"></span> are constants to be found.</p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></li><li>Hence show that the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span> coordinates of the turning points of the curve are solutions of the equation<div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x=\\frac{2\\mathrm e^{3x}-4}{\\mathrm e^{3x}+4}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol><p>The equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x=\\dfrac{2\\mathrm e^{3x}-4}{\\mathrm e^{3x}+4}\"></span> has two positive roots <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\beta\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\beta&gt;\\alpha\"></span></p><p>A student uses the iteration formula</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"x_{n+1}=\\frac{2\\mathrm e^{3x_n}-4}{\\mathrm e^{3x_n}+4}\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p>in an attempt to find approximations for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\beta\"></span></p><p>Diagram 1 shows a plot of part of the curve with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=\\dfrac{2\\mathrm e^{3x}-4}{\\mathrm e^{3x}+4}\"></span> and part of the line with equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y=x\"></span></p><figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:70mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-9ma0-01-2023-june/q15-figure.svg\" alt=\"Diagram 1. Axes x and y with origin O; part of the curve y = (2e^(3x) - 4)/(e^(3x) + 4) and part of the line y = x, crossing at x = alpha and x = beta; x = 1 is marked on the x-axis.\"></figure><p>Using Diagram 1 on page 42</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"3\"><li>draw a staircase diagram to show that the iteration formula starting with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=1\"></span> can be used to find an approximation for <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\beta\"></span> <span class=\"marks\">(1)</span></li></ol><p>Use the iteration formula with <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_1=1\"></span>, to find, to 3 decimal places,</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"4\"><li><ol class=\"parts\" type=\"i\"><li>the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x_2\"></span></li><li>the value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\beta\"></span></li></ol><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></li></ol><p>Using a suitable interval and a suitable function that should be stated</p><ol class=\"parts\" start=\"5\"><li>show that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\alpha=0.432\"></span> to 3 decimal places. <span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></li></ol>",
      "steps": [
